    "question": {
      ":question/id": "07716881-0eaf-5a42-882d-837350e8dd6a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which ordinary definite integral represents $\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(- 2 x + 2 y)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 x y)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t^{4})\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2]$?\n\nUse the supplied parameterization and limits. Select the integral whose integrand is $\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)$; do not evaluate it.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=t^{3}$ and $y=t^{4}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))&=(- 2 (t^{3}) + 2 (t^{4}))\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(2 (t^{3}) (t^{4}))\\,\\mathbf{j}\\\\&=(2 t^{4} - 2 t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{7})\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})=3 t^{2},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{4})=4 t^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(2 t^{4} - 2 t^{3})(3 t^{2})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{7})(4 t^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)=8 t^{10} + 6 t^{6} - 6 t^{5}.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(2 t^{4} - 2 t^{3})(3 t^{2})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{7})(4 t^{3})\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
