      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the vector line-integral formula:\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the coordinates $x=t^{3}$ and $y=t^{2}$ into both field components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))&=(- (t^{3}) + 2 (t^{2}))\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(2 (t^{3}) (t^{2}))\\,\\mathbf{j}\\\\&=(- t^{3} + 2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{5})\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each path component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{3})=3 t^{2},\\\\y^{\\prime}(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})=2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply matching components and add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\\\&=(- t^{3} + 2 t^{2})(3 t^{2})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{5})(2 t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the products:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)=4 t^{6} - 3 t^{5} + 6 t^{4}.\n$$\n\nKeep the supplied parameter limits. The required integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2}\\bigl[(- t^{3} + 2 t^{2})(3 t^{2})\\\\&\\quad+(2 t^{5})(2 t)\\bigr]\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
